course: dictionary
lesson: 15247
title: One word, three meanings: shiner
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A shiner is a noun, and it can mean three different things. The words around it show you which meaning the writer chose. Look for clues before you decide.
explain: «After the football match, Sam came home with a shiner.» The clues are football and came home with. A shiner here is a black eye, a bruise round the eye from a punch or a knock. This is an informal word, so you hear it in chatty talk more than in formal writing.
explain: «The new silver coin was a bright shiner in the sunlight.» The clues are bright and sunlight. Here a shiner is something that shines. Ask yourself: what word would fit in this sentence? Shiny thing fits, so that is the meaning.
explain: «The angler caught a small shiner and put it back in the lake.» Angler and lake point to fishing. In North America, a shiner is a little silvery fish. When context is not enough, a dictionary settles it.
fact: A shiner is a noun. Its plural is shiners.
fact: «Shiner» can mean a black eye: a bruise round the eye from a punch or a knock.
fact: «Shiner» can also mean something that shines, like a shiny coin.
fact: In North America, a shiner is a small silver fish.
fact: «Give someone a shiner» means to hit someone so that they get a black eye. It is informal, so use it in chatty speech, not in formal writing.
exercise: «After the football match, Sam came home with a shiner.» What is a shiner here? | A football team | A small silver fish | * A black eye from a knock | A bright, shiny coin
exercise: «The new silver coin was a bright shiner in the sunlight.» What does shiner mean here? | A kind of fish | A bruise from a punch | A dark cloud | * A bright, shiny thing
exercise: What is the plural of shiner? | * shiners | shinys | shiner's | shinees
test: «The angler caught a small shiner and put it back in the lake.» What is a shiner here? | A black eye | * A small silver fish | A rowing boat | A shiny coin
test: Lily said, «Don't give your brother a shiner!» What does shiner mean? | * A black eye from a punch | A bright light | A shiny sweet | A fishing rod
exam: «He came home with a real shiner after the fight.» Which meaning fits best, and what clue tells you? | * A black eye, because of the fight | A football, because of the match | A small silver fish, because of the lake | A shiny coin, because of the light
